# Commit messages

Use Conventional Commits. One subject line, under 100 characters:

`type: short imperative description`

Types:

- `feat`: a new feature
- `fix`: a bug fix
- `docs`: documentation only
- `style`: formatting or whitespace, no behavior change
- `refactor`: a code change that is not a fix or a feature
- `perf`: a performance improvement
- `test`: tests only
- `build`: the build system or dependencies
- `ci`: CI configuration
- `chore`: maintenance that fits none of the types above

- Lowercase type, colon, single space
- Imperative present tense (`add`, `fix`, `update`)
- No trailing period
- English
- Do not list files or restate the diff

```
fix: correct workout stat calculation
feat: add weekly progress chart
```
